# SmartSPIM Pipeline Dispatcher — Environment Configuration
#
# ── How to use this file ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Copy this file:
#      cp .env.example code/.env
#    Then fill in the values for your environment.
#    The dispatcher loads .env automatically at startup (existing shell
#    environment variables always take precedence over .env values).
#
# 2. In Code Ocean, set these as capsule environment variables instead of
#    using a .env file — Code Ocean injects them before the capsule runs.
#
# Any variable left blank disables the corresponding feature; the dispatcher
# logs a warning and continues without it.
#
# ── Three ways to pass parameters ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Parameters can be set in three ways (higher items win):
#
#   1. Named CLI flags  ->  ./run dispatch --cloud-mode false --output-path /scratch
#   2. Positional args  ->  ./run dispatch false /scratch/output /scratch/raw  (Nextflow)
#   3. Env var / .env   ->  CLOUD_MODE=false OUTPUT_PATH=/scratch ./run dispatch
#
# Positional order (mode-dependent):
#   split_channels:  <mode> [<cloud>] [<input_path>] [<output_path>]
#   other modes:     <mode> [<cloud>] [<output_path>] [<input_path>]
#
# Named flags and their env-var equivalents:
#
#   CLI flag                Env var              Description
#   ─────────────────────── ──────────────────── ────────────────────────────
#   --cloud-mode            CLOUD_MODE           true | false
#   --output-path           OUTPUT_BUCKET        S3 bucket (cloud) or …
#                           OUTPUT_PATH          … local root dir (local)
#   --input-path            INPUT_BUCKET         Raw-data S3 bucket (cloud) or …
#                           INPUT_PATH           … raw-data root dir (local);
#                                                defaults to the output location
#   --data-folder           DATA_FOLDER          Override ../data default
#   --results-folder        RESULTS_FOLDER       Override ../results default
#   --ng-base-url           NG_BASE_URL          Neuroglancer base URL
#   --ccf-annotation-s3     CCF_ANNOTATION_S3    CCF annotation S3 path
#   --co-domain             CODEOCEAN_DOMAIN     Code Ocean domain
#
# Run  ./run dispatch --help  to see the full CLI reference.
#
# ── Quick-start: SLURM / local mode ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   CLOUD_MODE=false
#   OUTPUT_PATH=/path/to/shared/storage
#   DATA_FOLDER=/path/to/dataset/input
#   RESULTS_FOLDER=/path/to/dataset/results
#   # Leave CUSTOM_KEY, API_SECRET, CODEOCEAN_DOMAIN blank to disable cloud
#   # integrations — the pipeline will still process and copy data locally.
#
# ── Quick-start: Code Ocean / AWS ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   CLOUD_MODE=true
#   OUTPUT_BUCKET=my-s3-bucket-name
#   CODEOCEAN_DOMAIN=https://codeocean.your-org.org
#   API_SECRET=<your Code Ocean API token>
#   CUSTOM_KEY=<MS Teams webhook URL>
#   SES_TOKEN_PATH=<Secrets Manager path>
#   SMARTSHEET_ID=<integer sheet ID>
#   SOURCE_EMAIL=pipeline@your-org.org
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Execution mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to false to run without AWS — all file operations use the local
# filesystem instead of S3.  Defaults to true (AWS / Code Ocean behaviour).
# CLI equivalent: second positional arg or --cloud-mode flag.
CLOUD_MODE=true

# ── Storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# S3 bucket where processed data is written (used when CLOUD_MODE=true).
# Can also be passed positionally (see order above) or via --output-path.
OUTPUT_BUCKET=

# Local root directory where the organised dataset is written (used when
# CLOUD_MODE=false, e.g. for SLURM runs on a shared filesystem).
# Can also be passed positionally (see order above) or via --output-path.
OUTPUT_PATH=

# S3 bucket holding the raw acquisition data (used when CLOUD_MODE=true;
# consumed by the split_channels mode to list the dataset channels).
# Can also be passed positionally (see order above) or via --input-path.
# Leave blank to read the raw data from OUTPUT_BUCKET.
INPUT_BUCKET=

# Local root directory holding the raw acquisition data (used when
# CLOUD_MODE=false). Leave blank to read the raw data from OUTPUT_PATH.
# Can also be passed positionally (see order above) or via --input-path.
INPUT_PATH=

# ── Path overrides (SLURM / non-Code-Ocean environments) ──────────────────────
# Override the Code Ocean default paths (../data and ../results).
# Leave blank to use the Code Ocean convention.
# CLI equivalent: --data-folder / --results-folder flags.
DATA_FOLDER=
RESULTS_FOLDER=

# ── Code Ocean ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your Code Ocean organisation domain (e.g. https://codeocean.your-org.org).
# If unset, Code Ocean data-asset registration is skipped.
# CLI equivalent: --co-domain flag.
CODEOCEAN_DOMAIN=

# Code Ocean API token — required for the dispatch mode.
API_SECRET=

# ── Notifications ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MS Teams webhook URL for pipeline-completion alerts.
# If unset, Teams alerts are silently skipped.
CUSTOM_KEY=

# AWS Secrets Manager path to the SES / Smartsheet API token.
# If unset, email alerts are silently skipped.
SES_TOKEN_PATH=

# Smartsheet sheet ID (integer) used to look up investigator email addresses.
SMARTSHEET_ID=

# SES-verified source address for outgoing pipeline notification emails.
SOURCE_EMAIL=

# ── Visualisation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL used when generating Neuroglancer links.
# Defaults to the public Google demo instance if unset.
# Set to empty string to disable Neuroglancer link generation entirely.
# CLI equivalent: --ng-base-url flag.
NG_BASE_URL=https://neuroglancer-demo.appspot.com/

# Full S3 path (including neuroglancer-precomputed suffix) to a precomputed
# CCF annotation volume for the CCF-overlay Neuroglancer layer.
# If unset, the CCF annotation layer is omitted from generated links.
# CLI equivalent: --ccf-annotation-s3 flag.
CCF_ANNOTATION_S3=s3://tissuecyte-visualizations/data/221205/ccf_annotations/|neuroglancer-precomputed:
